OOXML math reads a run's hyphen as the minus sign

Outside an m:nor (normal text) run Word renders an OMML hyphen as
U+2212, literal and double-struck runs included. The importer
escaped it as quoted StarMath text, so export wrote it back as
normal text (m:lit, m:nor) and Word kept a hyphen (Ely R15.11b).
Read it as MS_MINUS, StarMath's own minus; normal-text runs keep
their hyphen.
diff --git a/starmath/source/ooxmlimport.cxx b/starmath/source/ooxmlimport.cxx
index defd7388f..d937eb91e 100644
--- a/starmath/source/ooxmlimport.cxx
+++ b/starmath/source/ooxmlimport.cxx
@@ -612,6 +612,9 @@ OUString SmOoxmlImport::handleR()
                 isTagT = true;
                 XmlStream::Tag rtag = m_rStream.ensureOpeningTag( M_TOKEN( t ));
                 OUString sTagText = rtag.text;
+                // Outside normal text a hyphen is the minus sign.
+                if (!normal)
+                    sTagText = sTagText.replace('-', MS_MINUS);
                 if (scrString == "double-struck")
                 {
                     sTagText = SmOoxmlImport::handleSetString(sTagText);
